      <blockquote><p>Maybe add some easy but useful special cases to Lemma 07ZA:</p>
<p>One could add a new item 
"If <script type="math/tex">I</script> is an ideal of <script type="math/tex">R</script>, then <script type="math/tex">\operatorname{Fit}_0(R/I)=I</script>."</p>
<p>In (2), after "we have" and before the formula one could insert
"<script type="math/tex">\operatorname{Fit}_0(M \oplus M') = \operatorname{Fit}_0(M) \operatorname{Fit}_0(M')</script> and more generally"
(I think that that is the most commonly used case of (2)).</p>
<p>In the proof of (4), it would be good to put <script type="math/tex">n-k</script> in parentheses, twice.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
